# Root build-context excludes.
#
# SCOPE WARNING: Docker reads .dockerignore from the root of the *build
# context*, not from the repo root. Every context in docker-compose.yml is a
# subdirectory (./backend, ./sync, ./rsync), so this file is currently INERT --
# see backend/.dockerignore and sync/.dockerignore for the ones that take
# effect today.
#
# It is kept because a root context is the likely shape of the next change:
# a models package shared by backend/ and sync/ (Phase 1) cannot be COPYed from
# a subdirectory context, and moving `context:` to `.` would otherwise ship the
# whole repo -- .git, tests/, frontend/, data/ -- into the image.

# VCS
.git/
.gitignore
.github/

# Secrets and local state
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/.credentials
docker-compose.override.yml

# Python build/test artifacts
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info
**/.venv
**/venv
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.coverage
**/.coverage.*
**/htmlcov
**/coverage.xml

# Tests and tooling config: not needed at runtime in any image
**/tests
pyproject.toml

# Not part of any application image
data/
docs/
scripts/
nginx/
rsync/
LICENSE
README.md
CONTRIBUTING.md
CLAUDE.md
.claude/
docker-compose*.yml

# Editor / OS noise
**/.vscode
**/.idea
**/*.swp
**/*.swo
**/*~
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
**/*.log
